# Reference Section Content

Tables for looking a form up. Reference teaches nothing: every rule is explained in a guide (`src/routes/guides/`), and each table here links to the guide section that teaches it. Public: no auth guard.

## Route Structure

```
/reference                    Landing page (SectionIndex)
/reference/:tab               $tab.tsx: pronouns, articles, nouns, adjectives
/reference/verbs              verbs/route.tsx layout (own route family, not a :tab)
/reference/verbs/             redirects to /reference/verbs/present
/reference/verbs/:band        present, past, past-continuous, future
```

- `$tab.tsx` checks `VALID_TABS`; any other `:tab` throws `notFound()` (404).
- `MOVED_TO_GUIDES` in `$tab.tsx` redirects the tabs whose teaching moved into guides, so old links keep working:
  - /reference/cases → /guides/roles
  - /reference/prepositions → /guides/place
  - /reference/patterns → /guides/little-words#likes
- `head` sets the document title from the tab's `REFERENCE_TABS` label; a verb band's title is "Verbs: <band label>".
- Every tab and band renders `ReferenceNav` (a `NavTabs` bar over `REFERENCE_TABS`) above its content.

## Page shape

Every tab and verb band has the same shape, from `components/lookup-section.tsx`:

- `LookupPage`: `PageHeading` with the title and the one line "Tables for looking a form up. The rules are in the guides."
- One `LookupSection` per table, in a fixed order: an `h2`, a `GrammarTable` of `GreekText` cells with no case colours, and "Taught in: <guide section title> →" links.
- Nothing else: no hero, teaching cards, quizzes, mistakes or next-step cards.

`TAUGHT_IN` in `lookup-section.tsx` holds every guide section a table links to, with its title copied from the guide, so the pages never import the guide data. `src/routes/guides/guide-forms.test.ts` checks each entry against the guide's real section id and title.

## Landing Page

<route path="/reference">
<file>src/routes/reference/index.tsx</file>
<displays>
- `SectionIndex`: title "Reference", lede "Grammar patterns and paradigms"
- Ruled rows, Greek name first:
  - The case system: Αντωνυμίες / Pronouns
  - Words that agree: Άρθρα / Articles, Ουσιαστικά / Nouns, Επίθετα / Adjectives
  - Building sentences: Ρήματα / Verbs ("Every tense, by verb family")
</displays>
</route>

## Tabs

<tab route="/reference/pronouns" file="tabs/pronouns.tsx">
One table, "Every pronoun form", from `constants/pronouns.ts` (nothing generates pronouns). Links to little-words: forms, objects, long forms.
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/articles" file="tabs/nouns-articles.tsx">
One table, "The article, every form", rendered from `getArticle` (`src/lib/greek-grammar.ts`) through `gender-case-table.tsx`. Links to roles: articles, plural.
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/nouns" file="tabs/nouns.tsx">
One table per gender, from `AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS` (`constants/agreement.ts`, the same source as `declineNoun`), each pattern with example words from the DB (`getNounsForParadigmReference`, loaded by `$tab.tsx`). Links to the nouns guide's family sections.
</tab>

<tab route="/reference/adjectives" file="tabs/adjectives.tsx">
Three tables from `declineAdjective` (`src/lib/adjective-declension.ts`): καλός (-ος, -η, -ο), ωραίος (-ος, -α, -ο), βαρύς (-ύς, -ιά, -ύ). Links to the agreement guide.
</tab>

## Verb bands

<route path="/reference/verbs/:band">
<file>src/routes/reference/verbs/$band.tsx; tables in components/verbs-section.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: `getReferenceVerbsFn` (`src/server/fns/reference-verbs.ts`) loads every tense of the band's example verbs (`bandLemmas`).</data-source>
<displays>
`BAND_TABLES` lists each band's tables, their example verbs and the guide section each links to. The families follow the verbs guide:

- present: γράφω, μιλάω and the πάω set; πάω and τρώω endings; stressed -ώ; -μαι; -άμαι; είμαι
- past: simple past endings; stems with σ, ψ and ξ; four groups with a past of their own; -μαι; είμαι
- past continuous: regular; -άω and -ώ; verbs that add γ; own-past verbs; -μαι; είμαι
- future: θα and the short form; three sets of own short forms; two tables with no separate short form; -μαι
</displays>
<note>`src/routes/guides/guide-verb-forms.test.ts` checks the guides' verb tables against `generateConjugations`.</note>
</route>
